  nonce: 27a8  # 27a8
  message: "L1 AND L3 ARE CLOSED WITH BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE. L2 IS STILL LIVE. Item stays\nviolated on L2 alone.\n\nLive probes against production _ddg_taint_reaches, all controls passing (earned\nFalse via fmt.Printf -> False; earned False via closed cycle -> False; earned\nTrue -> True):\n  L1 barren definition: this item's own filed repro `f,[1],[9],{}` -> None.\n     A barren seed beside a closed chain -> None. CLOSED (PR #199).\n  L3 (WI-votom dual-role statement): uncatalogued beside-call -> None,\n     catalogued-terminating -> False. CLOSED.\n  L2 partially-recorded definition (the item's own faithful repro):\n     gate OFF -> False; gate ON -> None; control with the use recorded -> True.\n     STILL LIVE.\n\nWHY L2 IS STILL LIVE, precisely: WI-joluk's `forfeit_refutation` IS wired\n(2edbc6a2c1) but ONLY to the barrier arm (taint.py:2792). The §3a arm\n(taint.py:~2735) passes nothing, so a partially-recorded definition still\nreturns False there.\n\nBLAST RADIUS TODAY IS ZERO, and wiring forfeit into the §3a arm today is a\nNO-OP: that arm tests `is True`, so False -> None changes nothing. 0 of 68\nproduction §3a walks return False at all. If §3a ever gains removal authority\nthe gate would forfeit 29/31 pretix walked functions (93.5%) and 1/1 mitmproxy.\n\nTHEREFORE: do NOT spend a cycle wiring it now. Land the §3a-arm forfeit IN THE\nSAME PR as any §3a removal authority -- PR #214 makes each unearned False DELETE\na flow, so the ordering is load-bearing.\n\nSECOND RESIDUAL: cfg.uncovered_call_lines keys on CALL nodes only, so a def/use\nomission at a non-call construct is invisible to the gate. Read from cfg.py:1457,\nNOT measured.\n\nCLOSURE EVIDENCE THIS ITEM WILL NEED: a live repro on a REAL REPO where a\nbarrier walk returns False on a partially-recorded def and the gate flips it to\nNone. Fixtures do not close it -- both existing demonstrations of barrier-arm\nbehaviour are fixtures, and 0 production barrier walks have ever been observed."  # 27a8
